## Summary
- Use own-key checks when flattening MCP loopback union schema properties.
- Keep required fields only when the flattened schema defines an own property for that key.
- Add focused regression coverage for Object prototype property names such as toString.

## What Problem This Solves
MCP loopback tools can expose JSON schema properties with names like toString or constructor. Current main uses key in mergedProps while flattening anyOf/oneOf schemas, so Object.prototype keys are treated as already present even when the flattened schema has no own property. That can drop the actual property schema while still leaving the key in required.

## Evidence
Real environment tested: Local OpenClaw checkout on Linux, Node.js v22.22.0, using a real buildMcpToolSchema invocation against a loopback tool schema.

Before fix on current main, this input:
~~~js
buildMcpToolSchema([{
  name: 'proof_tool',
  description: 'proof',
  parameters: {
    anyOf: [{
      type: 'object',
      properties: { toString: { type: 'string' } },
      required: ['toString'],
    }],
  },
}]);
~~~

produced a warning and omitted the own toString property:
~~~text
mcp loopback: conflicting schema definitions for "toString", keeping the first variant
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {},
  "required": [
    "toString"
  ]
}
own toString: false
value type: function
~~~

After fix on this branch, the same real schema projection keeps the property as an own key:
~~~text
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "toString": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "toString"
  ]
}
own toString: true
value: {"type":"string"}
~~~

The focused regression also covers the inverse case where a required field names toString but no variant defines that property. The fixed code no longer keeps that inherited prototype name in required.

## Verification
- node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/mcp-http.schema.test.ts -- --reporter=verbose - passed, 4 gateway projects / 8 tests.
- git diff --check - passed.
- Collision check: open PR changed-file search found no open PR modifying src/gateway/mcp-http.schema.ts or src/gateway/mcp-http.schema.test.ts. I avoided src/gateway/mcp-http.test.ts because other open PRs touch it.
